  "content": {
    "id": "p89-task-7-14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Classify the following as either positive or negative hyperbolas.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p89-task-7-14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{3}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Positive.",
          "worked": "The reciprocal coefficient is $k=3>0$, so the hyperbola is positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p89-task-7-14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=-\\frac{4}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Negative.",
          "worked": "The reciprocal coefficient is $k=-4<0$, so the hyperbola is negative.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p89-task-7-14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{2}{x-5}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Positive.",
          "worked": "In $y=\\frac{a}{x-h}+k$, the coefficient is $a=2>0$. The translation does not change the branch orientation, so the hyperbola is positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p89-task-7-14-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{x+1}{x+2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Negative.\n\nThe point $(0,\\frac12)$ lies below $y=1$ and to the right of $x=-2$.",
          "worked": "The vertical asymptote is $x=-2$, from $x+2=0$. The horizontal asymptote is $y=1$, using the ratio of leading coefficients.\n\nAt $x=0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{0+1}{0+2}\\\\y&=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nThe point $(0,\\frac12)$ is to the right of $x=-2$ and below $y=1$. The right branch is below the horizontal asymptote, so the hyperbola is negative.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p89-task-7-14-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{2x+3}{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Positive.\n\nThe point $(0,3)$ lies above $y=2$ and to the right of $x=-1$.",
          "worked": "The vertical asymptote is $x=-1$, from $x+1=0$. The horizontal asymptote is $y=2$, using the ratio of leading coefficients.\n\nAt $x=0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{2(0)+3}{0+1}\\\\y&=3\\end{align*}$$\nThe point $(0,3)$ is to the right of $x=-1$ and above $y=2$. The right branch is above the horizontal asymptote, so the hyperbola is positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p89-task-7-14-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{3x-2}{2x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Negative.\n\nThe point $(0,-2)$ lies below $y=\\frac32$ and to the right of $x=-\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "The vertical asymptote is $x=-\\frac12$, from $2x+1=0$. The horizontal asymptote is $y=\\frac32$, using the ratio of leading coefficients.\n\nAt $x=0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{3(0)-2}{2(0)+1}\\\\y&=-2\\end{align*}$$\nThe point $(0,-2)$ is to the right of $x=-\\frac12$ and below $y=\\frac32$. The right branch is below the horizontal asymptote, so the hyperbola is negative.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p89-task-7-14-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{5-x}{x+4}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Positive.\n\nThe point $(0,\\frac54)$ lies above $y=-1$ and to the right of $x=-4$.",
          "worked": "The vertical asymptote is $x=-4$, from $x+4=0$. The horizontal asymptote is $y=-1$, using the ratio of leading coefficients.\n\nAt $x=0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{5-0}{0+4}\\\\y&=\\frac54\\end{align*}$$\nThe point $(0,\\frac54)$ is to the right of $x=-4$ and above $y=-1$. The right branch is above the horizontal asymptote, so the hyperbola is positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p89-task-7-14-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{5x+4}{2x+3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Negative.\n\nThe point $(0,\\frac43)$ lies below $y=\\frac52$ and to the right of $x=-\\frac32$.",
          "worked": "The vertical asymptote is $x=-\\frac32$, from $2x+3=0$. The horizontal asymptote is $y=\\frac52$, using the ratio of leading coefficients.\n\nAt $x=0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{5(0)+4}{2(0)+3}\\\\y&=\\frac43\\end{align*}$$\nThe point $(0,\\frac43)$ is to the right of $x=-\\frac32$ and below $y=\\frac52$. The right branch is below the horizontal asymptote, so the hyperbola is negative.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      }
    ]
  },
